  "description": "A seven-eighth dance with an extra breath in its last step. Birch Reservoir\u2019s opening rises into G minor; compact lower chords sway beneath a melody that breaks free into single notes. The middle shifts the long step to the beginning, then a quiet return gathers the melody back into chords.",
